message.content:
You are fixing one frontend performance problem in inkling, an Electron + React + TypeScript + Vite app (Bun 1.4.2). Read AGENTS.md at the worktree root first. Its rules apply.

WORKSPACE: C:\Users\chris\.t3\worktrees\inkling\perf-library-io (branch perf/library-io). Work ONLY there. Three other agents are editing this same worktree right now, and two of them touch src/App.tsx (capture code and video cards). Make targeted edits with the Edit tool only and NEVER rewrite src/App.tsx with Write. If an edit fails because the text moved, re-read and retry. Run NO git commands that change state (no add, commit, checkout, stash, reset or restore). The maintainer commits. Do not launch dev servers or Electron.

TASK: Settings has an Archive tab. In src/App.tsx, find `loadArchivedItems`, near the Settings effect that loads the app version and library size. Every time Settings opens, it fetches every archived item (listArchivedItems) plus processing summaries for all of them (getProcessingSummaries), and the Archive tab renders every archived card at once with no virtualization.
1. Load archived items only when the Archive tab is actually shown, not when Settings opens on another tab. Reload after a restore or permanent delete, the way it does now. Fetch processing summaries only if the archive UI actually uses them. If it does, fetch them only for what's rendered, or drop the call if it's unused.
2. Virtualize the archive grid so only cards near the visible part of its scroll container render. First look at how the main library grid virtualizes in App.tsx (search for virtualization / GRID_GAP / TARGET_CARD_WIDTH / visible range logic) and reuse that approach or helper. Do not add a dependency.
3. Keep everything else working:
   - restore;
   - permanent delete;
   - any select-all or empty-archive actions;
   - the empty state;
   - keyboard focus;
   - the current look of the Archive tab. Do not restyle it.

If you extract a pure helper (e.g. a visible-range calculation), add a small focused bun test for it. Don't write render-to-markup tests. Run `bunx biome check src/App.tsx <other changed files>`, `bun test <test files you touched>`, and `bun run typecheck`. Check the exit code with `echo $?`, not through a pipe. If typecheck errors are only in code another agent is editing (capture, video posters, electron/), say so instead of fixing them.

REPORT (under 150 words): what changed, when the archive loads now, how virtualization works, whether processing summaries are still fetched, checks run with results, and anything left unfinished.

